1
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:14,200
That guy is like the sun.

2
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,800
Bright and warm.

3
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,300
No matter where he goes,

4
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,800
he can instantly make everyone smile.

5
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:39,633
I could never reach that light.

6
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:50,733
That's what I always thought.

7
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:07,100
Suzuki, do you like me?

8
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:15,433
Suzuki.

9
00:01:16,933 --> 00:01:18,667
Look at me.

10
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:20,933
Answer me.

11
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:25,833
How did it end up like this?

12
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:32,300
Is this a dream?

13
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:35,100
Or...

14
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,867
(Episode 1)

15
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,533
(Alarm / Snooze)

16
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:57,800
Oh crap!

17
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:06,633
I'm Suzuki Hajime, a high school sophomore.

18
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:10,167
My hobbies are daydreaming
and writing novels.

19
00:02:16,633 --> 00:02:18,767
And my absolute favorite thing is BL.

20
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,333
I'm what you'd call a fudanshi.

21
00:02:24,967 --> 00:02:29,033
But at the end of the
day, BL is just a hobby.

22
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:33,200
I've never actually had a
crush on a guy in real life.

23
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,767
Besides, romance and stuff like that

24
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:45,033
has absolutely nothing
to do with a guy like me.

25
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:51,000
Let's be real, to girls,

26
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:53,400
I might as well be invisible.

27
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:54,233
Um...

28
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:56,867
He gave this to me!

29
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:59,267
No way! What are you talking about?

30
00:02:59,367 --> 00:03:01,033
- Um...
- No way!

31
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:03,167
I can't do it.

32
00:03:03,267 --> 00:03:04,733
Absolutely not.

33
00:03:08,667 --> 00:03:11,767
I gave up on that a long time ago.

34
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:15,800
About last time...

35
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,233
I know, right?

36
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:21,400
- Oh crap.
- Time to study.

37
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:27,000
Honestly, I don't even have any friends.

38
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,800
I'm a total loner.

39
00:03:42,767 --> 00:03:46,133
But there's a group of guys in my class

40
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:50,067
who live in a completely
different world than me.

41
00:03:57,667 --> 00:03:58,900
Stylish,

42
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:05,400
outgoing, and super popular.

43
00:04:06,867 --> 00:04:09,027
"Saeki Yuma / 184 Posts
32K Followers / 357 Following."

44
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,409
- Morning, Haru-chan.
- Morning!

45
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:14,267
Huh? Did you change your makeup today?

46
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:16,833
Yeah, does it look weird?

47
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:19,133
Not at all, it's super cute.

48
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:24,567
Hey, you lovebirds! Showing
off bright and early, huh?

49
00:04:25,133 --> 00:04:27,333
My Muscles's getting jealous.

50
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:30,067
Hey! Don't call me "Muscles."

51
00:04:30,667 --> 00:04:31,933
Call me a macho man.

52
00:04:32,033 --> 00:04:32,733
Same difference.

53
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:33,833
It's the same thing.

54
00:04:33,933 --> 00:04:35,700
No it's not! It's totally different!

55
00:04:38,133 --> 00:04:39,900
Iwasaki Shun.

56
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:41,867
Judo club member.

57
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,867
The strong, reliable, athletic hottie.

58
00:04:45,967 --> 00:04:48,233
I can't believe he won
just like that. He's amazing!

59
00:04:48,333 --> 00:04:48,933
Yes!

60
00:04:49,033 --> 00:04:50,543
As expected from the prefectural champ.

61
00:04:50,567 --> 00:04:52,733
He might even represent Japan someday.

62
00:04:55,067 --> 00:04:56,067
That's so cool.

63
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:58,767
Iwasaki, did you do the math homework?

64
00:04:59,733 --> 00:05:01,400
Crap, I forgot.

65
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,333
Takeuchi.

66
00:05:03,633 --> 00:05:05,033
Let me copy yours.

67
00:05:05,133 --> 00:05:07,033
No way, do it yourself.

68
00:05:07,133 --> 00:05:08,833
Takeuchi Tomoaki.

69
00:05:10,067 --> 00:05:13,333
The calm, collected, and brilliant hottie.

70
00:05:13,667 --> 00:05:16,500
Damn, this guy's got it in the bag.

71
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,367
I heard Takeuchi

72
00:05:18,467 --> 00:05:21,200
always ranks in the top ten
nationally on mock exams.

73
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,400
Seriously?

74
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,140
When does he even find the time to study?

75
00:05:24,167 --> 00:05:26,133
He's a total genius.

76
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,967
Alright, everyone back to your seats.

77
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:31,933
Homeroom is starting.

78
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:34,333
By the way, where's Serizawa?

79
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:37,967
Don't tell me... he's late?

80
00:05:39,367 --> 00:05:40,867
And then...

81
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:53,067
Hey! How's it going?

82
00:05:53,367 --> 00:05:54,767
Serizawa Haruto.

83
00:05:54,867 --> 00:05:57,600
Serizawa, you're too loud
for this early in the morning.

84
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,133
And you're blatantly late.

85
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:01,167
Huh? I made it just in time, right?

86
00:06:01,267 --> 00:06:03,000
You're definitely out.

87
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,900
What? Seriously?

88
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,167
Come on, please?

89
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:07,267
No.

90
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:10,233
Mr. Bunny~.

91
00:06:11,033 --> 00:06:13,100
Playing cute won't work.

92
00:06:13,833 --> 00:06:14,867
Get to your seat.

93
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:16,333
Why not?

94
00:06:20,233 --> 00:06:26,433
They are the school's most popular
group, The Popular Clique's Big Four.

95
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:53,867
Nice job.

96
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,533
After starting my sophomore year,

97
00:06:56,867 --> 00:07:00,567
I ended up in the same class
as Serizawa for the first time.

98
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:03,067
And I was instantly captivated by him.

99
00:07:05,233 --> 00:07:07,033
He looks so handsome again today.

100
00:07:12,133 --> 00:07:15,333
Because to me, Serizawa is...

101
00:07:18,033 --> 00:07:20,067
my ideal seme.

102
00:07:23,767 --> 00:07:29,667
And right now, I'm writing
a BL novel based on him.

103
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:32,533
It's definitely in here.

104
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:35,267
Really? You said that yesterday too.

105
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:46,067
If anyone ever found out about my hobby...

106
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,600
It's nothing!

107
00:07:50,667 --> 00:07:51,667
Oops.

108
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,767
It's about time.

109
00:07:54,867 --> 00:07:56,700
Let's go.

110
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,733
Hurry up.

111
00:08:02,833 --> 00:08:04,233
Suzuki.

112
00:08:04,333 --> 00:08:06,100
Are you looking for something?

113
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:12,433
Se-Serizawa?

114
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,567
Um...

115
00:08:18,973 --> 00:08:21,973
Is this what you're looking for?

116
00:08:22,017 --> 00:08:22,764
[TN: Literally "For the Plot"]

117
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:27,400
Huh? H-How did you...

118
00:08:28,033 --> 00:08:29,633
We had an elective class today, right?

119
00:08:29,733 --> 00:08:32,567
It didn't have a name on
it, but it was at your desk.

120
00:08:32,667 --> 00:08:33,767
Here you go.

121
00:08:36,267 --> 00:08:38,867
So that's what happened.

122
00:08:40,867 --> 00:08:44,667
Th-Thank you.

123
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:56,200
So, this "Serizawa Haruto"
written in the notebook...

124
00:08:57,433 --> 00:08:58,700
Is that about me?

125
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:13,100
I'm doomed...

126
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:18,267
Suzuki?

127
00:09:19,833 --> 00:09:22,167
Hey, are you listening?

128
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,233
I'm sorry!

129
00:09:31,333 --> 00:09:33,133
The n-notebook...

130
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,867
♪ Love, love, love, love, whatever ♪

131
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:54,467
♪ Love, love, love, love, whatever ♪

132
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:58,533
♪ Where is the sky that
flies in the dead of night? ♪

133
00:09:58,633 --> 00:10:00,133
♪ Love, love, love, love, whatever ♪

134
00:10:00,233 --> 00:10:02,033
♪ An ambiguous day is fine by me ♪

135
00:10:02,133 --> 00:10:03,867
♪ You blurt it out ♪

136
00:10:03,967 --> 00:10:06,067
♪ But those eyes are bloodshot ♪

137
00:10:06,167 --> 00:10:07,607
♪ Love, love, love, love, whatever ♪

138
00:10:07,667 --> 00:10:09,367
♪ Stop talking about love and all that ♪

139
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:17,000
♪ Just swallow the tears
touched in an instant ♪

140
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:21,067
♪ And welcome the night
with a moistened throat ♪

141
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:25,166
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me."

142
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:28,400
Is Serizawa mad at me?

143
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:31,267
Ugh... What should I do?

144
00:10:31,367 --> 00:10:33,567
He's definitely mad.

145
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:40,800
No, worse than that... I'm afraid...

146
00:10:42,233 --> 00:10:44,467
Really? Did you hear?

147
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:46,000
No way, no way.

148
00:10:46,467 --> 00:10:49,100
Isn't Suzuki's hobby a bit much?

149
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,200
I know, right?

150
00:10:50,267 --> 00:10:52,067
Honestly, it creeps me out a bit.

151
00:10:52,167 --> 00:10:52,700
Same here.

152
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,600
Why would a guy be into BL?

153
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:55,533
That's so gross.

154
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:57,033
Maybe he's got his eye on you.

155
00:10:57,133 --> 00:10:58,800
- No way.
- Don't say that.

156
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,800
I'm just kidding.

157
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:02,000
But you two would make a cute couple.

158
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,533
I said no!

159
00:11:03,633 --> 00:11:04,767
That's awful.

160
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,900
Anyway, I need to apologize
to him properly first.

161
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,100
And get my notebook back.

162
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,700
It's fine, it's fine.

163
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,333
I can totally do this.

164
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:41,533
I got this, I got this.

165
00:11:47,867 --> 00:11:49,167
Okay.

166
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:54,333
One more time.

167
00:11:54,433 --> 00:11:55,933
Okay.

168
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:57,267
This way?

169
00:11:57,367 --> 00:11:58,700
Or this way?

170
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,200
No, no, no.

171
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:03,100
No, absolutely not.

172
00:12:09,233 --> 00:12:11,933
Let's have a bento championship!

173
00:12:12,033 --> 00:12:13,600
Ready~.

174
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:17,500
That looks so good.

175
00:12:17,533 --> 00:12:23,300
I don't have the guts to
talk to those flashy guys.

176
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,009
- This bento is totally cheating!
- This bento is amazing!

177
00:12:25,033 --> 00:12:26,900
Right?

178
00:12:28,433 --> 00:12:31,033
Look for yourself.

179
00:12:31,133 --> 00:12:32,467
Oh, wow.

180
00:12:32,933 --> 00:12:34,500
Hurry up.

181
00:12:37,433 --> 00:12:39,133
Alright, let's get started.

182
00:12:39,233 --> 00:12:41,600
Pair up for warm-ups.

183
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,033
Who wants to pair up with me?

184
00:12:46,367 --> 00:12:47,233
Let's go.

185
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:49,200
- Okay.
- Hurry up.

186
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:51,600
Serizawa, let's pair up.

187
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,333
Sorry, I'll pass for now.

188
00:12:53,667 --> 00:12:55,100
Suzuki.

189
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,500
Wanna pair up with me?

190
00:12:58,700 --> 00:12:59,467
Huh?

191
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:01,333
Keep it up!

192
00:13:01,933 --> 00:13:02,933
Again.

193
00:13:02,967 --> 00:13:04,700
Ah! That hurts...

194
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:10,700
Why did Serizawa ask to pair up with me?

195
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:13,000
What the heck is going on?

196
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:18,733
Is he still mad about yesterday?

197
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,100
Huh? Takeuchi.

198
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,880
Why are you paired with the teacher today?

199
00:13:24,567 --> 00:13:26,800
Serizawa ditched me.

200
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,600
Huh?

201
00:13:29,533 --> 00:13:31,200
Poor you.

202
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:34,233
Hey, why? Pairing with
the teacher isn't that bad.

203
00:13:34,333 --> 00:13:35,433
Yeah... I guess.

204
00:13:35,533 --> 00:13:36,300
Hey, Takeuchi.

205
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,967
Ugh...

206
00:13:38,267 --> 00:13:39,533
This is...

207
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:41,000
A bit...

208
00:13:43,767 --> 00:13:47,467
Since when did Serizawa and Suzuki
get so close?

209
00:13:52,867 --> 00:13:54,367
Just mind your own business.

210
00:13:57,367 --> 00:14:04,567
I feel like everyone's
staring at us, and...

211
00:14:06,933 --> 00:14:10,200
We're way closer than I thought.

212
00:14:12,367 --> 00:14:15,067
Suzuki, are you okay?

213
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:17,700
Are you not feeling well?

214
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:24,333
No, I'm fine...

215
00:14:26,067 --> 00:14:31,500
But... your face is all red.

216
00:14:38,267 --> 00:14:41,900
I can't take this. I
just want to run away...

217
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,433
Sir, Suzuki doesn't look too well.

218
00:14:44,533 --> 00:14:46,300
Can I take him to the nurse's office?

219
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,600
Huh?

220
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:50,367
Sure, don't push yourself too hard.

221
00:14:50,467 --> 00:14:52,167
No, I...

222
00:14:52,367 --> 00:14:53,900
Come on, hop on.

223
00:14:55,033 --> 00:14:56,233
But...

224
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,833
Hurry up.

225
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:12,800
Serizawa...

226
00:15:12,833 --> 00:15:14,133
Yeah?

227
00:15:15,667 --> 00:15:16,833
I'm sorry.

228
00:15:16,933 --> 00:15:20,933
I'm... not actually sick.

229
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:23,133
I know.

230
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,900
Huh?

231
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,800
Then... where are we going now?

232
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,133
Somewhere we can be alone.

233
00:15:42,433 --> 00:15:43,800
The classroom?

234
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,267
Here we are.

235
00:15:51,133 --> 00:15:52,500
Thanks.

236
00:15:53,867 --> 00:15:57,300
You've been looking for a
chance to talk to me all day, right?

237
00:15:58,167 --> 00:16:01,267
So I figured it'd be better
if we were alone.

238
00:16:01,733 --> 00:16:03,100
Here you go.

239
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,200
Thanks.

240
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:17,300
Um... about this notebook.

241
00:16:37,167 --> 00:16:40,400
Suzuki, are you writing a BL novel?

242
00:16:43,767 --> 00:16:46,633
Yeah... you could say that.

243
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:51,433
Since you based a character on me...

244
00:16:51,533 --> 00:16:56,467
Could it be... Suzuki, do you like me?

245
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:07,067
Look at me, okay?

246
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:12,733
Answer me, Suzuki.

247
00:17:21,367 --> 00:17:22,667
I...

248
00:17:25,333 --> 00:17:26,467
I'm so sorry!

249
00:17:26,567 --> 00:17:27,433
Huh?

250
00:17:27,533 --> 00:17:29,833
Huh? What's wrong?

251
00:17:29,933 --> 00:17:34,833
I used you as a model without asking
and did something misleading.

252
00:17:35,433 --> 00:17:37,800
I'm really, truly sorry!

253
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,443
Anyway, just lift your head up first.

254
00:17:39,467 --> 00:17:41,633
I just like BL.

255
00:17:42,767 --> 00:17:43,867
I just like to fantasize.

256
00:17:43,967 --> 00:17:46,400
It'd be perfect if there was
a seme like you, Serizawa.

257
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:51,100
I may be a fudanshi,
but it's just a hobby.

258
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:53,333
I didn't mean it like that.

259
00:17:53,433 --> 00:17:57,667
So I don't see you in that way.

260
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,033
I see.

261
00:18:02,133 --> 00:18:05,433
Anyway, I'm sorry for
making you uncomfortable.

262
00:18:05,533 --> 00:18:07,400
I'll do whatever I can
to make it up to you.

263
00:18:09,667 --> 00:18:11,000
Make it up to me?

264
00:18:12,567 --> 00:18:14,143
Like... compensation for
emotional distress or something.

265
00:18:14,167 --> 00:18:16,167
I don't really have much
money on me, though.

266
00:18:17,733 --> 00:18:19,433
As long as it's something I can do...

267
00:18:19,533 --> 00:18:21,233
I'll do anything.

268
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,267
Anything?

269
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:25,167
Yeah.

270
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:30,333
So... please.

271
00:18:34,133 --> 00:18:37,367
Don't tell anyone else.

272
00:18:45,667 --> 00:18:46,867
Okay.

273
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:49,833
In that case...

274
00:18:58,733 --> 00:19:00,333
Let me be your first reader.

275
00:19:00,433 --> 00:19:02,567
Let me read your novel.

276
00:19:02,667 --> 00:19:03,967
Huh?

277
00:19:04,067 --> 00:19:06,467
Have you been misunderstanding
me this whole time?

278
00:19:06,567 --> 00:19:08,300
I'm not mad at all.

279
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,900
Actually, I'm pretty happy about it.

280
00:19:12,233 --> 00:19:13,267
Huh?

281
00:19:13,867 --> 00:19:16,167
Because I think of myself as a seme, too.

282
00:19:16,267 --> 00:19:17,667
Huh?

283
00:19:17,933 --> 00:19:19,567
Sorry, I should've told you sooner.

284
00:19:19,667 --> 00:19:21,833
I like BL, too.

285
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,333
What!

286
00:19:24,433 --> 00:19:26,367
Do you have to be that surprised?

287
00:19:26,467 --> 00:19:29,167
Because I can't believe
you like BL, Serizawa.

288
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:30,067
Why not?

289
00:19:30,167 --> 00:19:32,833
It doesn't matter who likes BL, right?

290
00:19:35,533 --> 00:19:38,067
By the way, what kind do you usually read?

291
00:19:38,167 --> 00:19:41,200
I've been really into
Ishibashi Tatakiware lately.

292
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,300
Especially his works.

293
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:43,400
Tatakiware?

294
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,743
I absolutely love his works, too!

295
00:19:44,767 --> 00:19:47,433
No way! We have the exact same taste!

296
00:19:47,533 --> 00:19:48,933
Yay!

297
00:19:51,433 --> 00:19:52,800
Yay!

298
00:19:56,467 --> 00:19:59,000
Now I want to read your novel even more.

299
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,733
Your novel.

300
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,233
No, well...

301
00:20:05,333 --> 00:20:06,809
Didn't you just say you'd do anything?

302
00:20:06,833 --> 00:20:11,067
But... it's not very good,
and it's not even finished.

303
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:16,900
I haven't shown it to anyone yet.

304
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,967
Then that makes me
Suzuki's very first reader.

305
00:20:21,067 --> 00:20:21,967
Huh?
"Huh?"

306
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,533
Please.

307
00:20:24,633 --> 00:20:29,500
Let me be Suzuki's first reader.

308
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,800
That sounded so cool...

309
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:38,267
What?

310
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:39,867
Did your heart skip a beat?

311
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:42,300
Yeah.

312
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:46,500
Ah, but...

313
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:49,533
Maybe it sounds better like this.

314
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:56,133
Give me your first time,
Suzuki, or something like that.

315
00:20:56,233 --> 00:20:58,733
What is that? That's amazing.

316
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:00,333
Let's try that again.

317
00:21:05,167 --> 00:21:07,067
Give it to me.

318
00:21:07,167 --> 00:21:10,133
Your first time, Suzuki.

319
00:21:16,033 --> 00:21:17,533
How was that?

320
00:21:23,667 --> 00:21:25,067
Suzuki?

321
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,300
Hello?

322
00:21:30,133 --> 00:21:31,700
What's wrong?

323
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:40,967
P-Perfect...

324
00:21:41,933 --> 00:21:43,667
What kind of reaction is that?

325
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:46,367
So, are you going to give it to me or not?

326
00:21:46,467 --> 00:21:48,633
Your first time, Suzuki.
Will you give it to me?

327
00:21:48,733 --> 00:21:51,533
Hurry up and decide. Pick one.

328
00:21:53,467 --> 00:21:55,700
If you don't mind...

329
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,433
I'll give it to you.

330
00:21:58,133 --> 00:22:00,000
Great, I'll gladly accept it.

331
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:12,600
You froze again.

332
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:16,533
Because... what you just said
was totally unfair, Serizawa.

333
00:22:17,633 --> 00:22:19,033
So cute.

334
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:25,400
And just like that, Serizawa
started reading my novel.

335
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:28,967
Then come to the rooftop
during lunch break tomorrow.

336
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:30,767
Okay.

337
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:36,867
But I didn't know it at the time.

338
00:22:38,667 --> 00:22:41,500
Popular Serizawa.

339
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:47,067
Acts Weird Around Me.

340
00:22:47,933 --> 00:22:49,967
(Next Episode)
Suzuki, Suzuki.

341
00:22:50,067 --> 00:22:52,433
Starting today,
let's eat lunch together every day.

342
00:22:52,533 --> 00:22:54,300
We're bonding right now.

343
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:58,267
Most semes are great cooks.
Leave it to me.

344
00:22:58,367 --> 00:23:00,300
I make a killer stew.

345
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:01,967
(This drama is purely fictional.)
Can I?
